   "body": "**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2, cloud/orch-r1259-fable, round 1): APPROVE** — head 9da2a741\n\nThe diff applies the single `ledger-note` of #1232 exactly: one line of `docs/CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md` (row 744, line 124), `MainWindow.swift:613-705` → `MainWindow.swift:683-706`, and nothing else.\n\nFindings (none blocking):\n\n1. **Detail** — `docs/CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md:124`. The range stops three lines short of the end of the logged-out block. At `87fe0d1c` the filter `Picker` is 683-695 with its modifiers on 696-698, and the `if !isLoggedIn { … }` block runs 699-709: 706 closes the `VStack`, 707-708 are its two `listRow…` modifiers, 709 closes the `if`. Both note strings (\"Connexion requise pour Favoris, Suivis et Lus\", \"Vous pouvez consulter \"Tous\" sans compte.\") are inside 683-706, so the proof holds. The note of #1232 asks for `683-706` verbatim, so the PR is right to write that; `683-709` would be the full block if a later note wants it.\n\n2. **Detail** — same row. The old range, read at `87fe0d1c`, happened to include the sub-forum picker (664-681), which the new range drops. The row's \"legacy perdait le sous-forum\" claim is still carried by `ObjCForumTopicsLoaderWorker.m:36-89`, so nothing is left unproven. No change needed.\n\n**Verified** (all run in the given checkout, read only):\n- `git diff origin/dev-swift...HEAD`: one file, +1/-1, `--check` clean, only the range token differs in the row.\n- #1232 body read with `gh api`: one `ledger-note` block, matching the change.\n- `git show 87fe0d1c:HFRswift/Swift/MainWindow.swift` lines 600-720: picker and logged-out note located as above.\n- `git show 2440d79:…MainWindow.swift`: the picker starts at 613 there, confirming the old range was `2440d79` lines.\n- Other citations of row 744 at `87fe0d1c`:\n  - `Favorites.swift:357` is the `ForumTopicsListView(` call carrying `initialFlagOverride: .favorites` (line 359). At `2440d79` line 357 is unrelated collapse-button code, so this is a genuine `87fe0d1c` line.\n  - `ObjCForumTopicsLoaderWorker.m:36-89` is exactly `forumURLBySettingOwnTopic:` plus `forumURLWithCatID:`; the file is unchanged between `2440d79` and `87fe0d1c`.\n- Neighbouring cases: no other `613-705` anywhere in `docs`, `tooling`, `App` or `Packages`. The two other `MainWindow.swift … @ 87fe0d1c` rows spot-checked (964: `:923-930` page-picker sheet; 994: `:1564-1567` `syncAppIconBadge`) match their text.\n\nNot run: the Docs consistency check (no local script found under `tooling/docs/`; CI is the arbiter). No tests or lint apply to a one-line docs change.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
